\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Washing Machine pentad should reach the Laundry chamber and begin its intervention as Sarah\'92s waters break.
\f1\b0 \strokec2  That puts it as close as possible: in position around the apparatus, beginning to act, but unable to complete the shutdown before the ending. The notes that leave it approaching the Laundry should give way to that staging.\

\f0\b \strokec2 The pentad threatening Eloise can serve the image you describe without an explained targeting rationale.
\f1\b0 \strokec2  Fridge Force\'92s purpose need not become fully legible. Its arrival turns Sarah and Eloise\'92s argument into an immediate physical threat, just as Chanta finally reaches Sarah. Keep the target clear through its positioning around Eloise; Sarah\'92s presence need not explain its arrival. My earlier objection treated an unexplained motive as something requiring repair. Here, that mystery can remain.\

\f0\b \strokec2 I see no necessary narrative reason for Sarah to interpret MoSES\'92s operating limits.
\f1\b0 \strokec2  That interpretation belongs to the escalation notes\'92 proposed technical argument; it needn\'92t survive into the confrontation. Sarah already has grounds to challenge Eloise through the historical research and Project Kebab. The drones can interrupt that argument rather than supply another premise for it.\
My observation about what Sarah could infer from five moving drones was therefore unnecessary to your staging. She happens to be beside their target. Her immediate problem is the threat, not diagnosing their engineering.\
